  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# 1.1.070626.1\n\nDate: 2026-07-06\n\n## Added\n\n- Added a public in-process workflow command surface through `IWorkflowCommandDispatcher` for backend and library callers that need to start workflows or operate workflow runs without going through HTTP routes.\n- Added `WorkflowCommandOptions`, `WorkflowCommandResult`, `WorkflowCommandStatus`, `WorkflowCommandRun`, `WorkflowCommandStep`, and `WorkflowRunAction` contracts for command dispatch, accepted/completed outcomes, authorization failures, and authorized run snapshots.\n- Added default-system and named-system workflow command dispatch so callers can target the same Workable systems used by worker command dispatch.\n- Added `IHttpContextWorkflowCommandDispatcher` for ASP.NET Core hosts that want workflow command dispatch using the current HTTP request context.\n\n## Changed\n\n- Routed the built-in workflow HTTP start and action routes through the shared in-process workflow command dispatcher so HTTP and backend command paths use the same command behavior.\n- Updated workflow docs to describe the in-process workflow command surface and avoid referring to it as a separate backend surface.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Preserved authorized completed workflow run snapshots in HTTP wait-for-completion responses even when the runtime can no longer rehydrate the run by id.\n- Prevented unauthorized HTTP workflow action responses from hydrating and serializing workflow run details by id.\n- Expanded workflow command and HTTP adapter test coverage for command status mapping, named systems, wait behavior, authorization, action handling, and command-result snapshots.",
